@using RenoTrack.Website.Content
@using RenoTrack.Website.Site
@inject CompanyIdentityOptions Company
@*
    The marketing header (D103; re-aligned in Slice 5v, D107; composed to the approved reference in Slice 5h).

    Composition: a brand zone bleeding to the left edge of the viewport, cut off by an angled edge, then the
    navigation and one prominent call to action on the right of a near-black band.

    The angle is drawn by a decorative pseudo-element behind the zone, never by clipping the zone itself: a
    clip-path on an element that contains a link would cut that link's focus ring off at the diagonal.

    The logo is decorative when it appears (alt=""): the company name sits beside it as real text. That differs
    from _CustomerLayout, where the logo replaces the name, because the web logo carries no wordmark (D103).

    **No logo is drawn in the brand zone, by rule.** The zone is painted in the accent colour, so a mark drawn in
    the brand's own colours loses whichever parts match it — the dark parts against a dark band, the accent parts
    against this one. Until the owner approves artwork for a known surface, the company name alone is the brand
    treatment (V-4/V-5), which is a finished design rather than a fallback. CompanyIdentity:LogoOnDarkPath stays
    the configured asset for dark surfaces and is used by the footer.

    The brand links to the homepage (D104); the name text gives the link its accessible name.

    The primary navigation renders only when SiteNavigation has entries, which are pages that exist. It is a plain
    list at every width: the narrow-screen <details> disclosure arrives when there are several real entries (D104).

    The call to action is the phone number, which is the strongest action this application actually has today. No
    button is drawn for a feature that does not exist.
*@
@{
    var currentPath = Context.Request.Path.Value ?? "/";
}
<header class="site-header">
    <div class="site-header-inner">
        <div class="site-brand-zone">
            <a class="site-brand" href="/">
                <span class="site-brand-name">@Company.DisplayName</span>
            </a>
        </div>

        <div class="site-header-actions">
            @if (SiteNavigation.Primary.Count > 0)
            {
                <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Hauptnavigation">
                    <ul class="site-nav-list">
                        @foreach (var item in SiteNavigation.Primary)
                        {
                            var isCurrent = string.Equals(currentPath, item.Href, StringComparison.Ordinal);
                            <li><a class="site-nav-link" href="@item.Href" aria-current="@(isCurrent ? "page" : null)">@item.Text</a></li>
                        }
                    </ul>
                </nav>
            }

            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Company.ContactPhone))
            {
                <a class="site-button site-header-call" href="@SiteFormatting.TelHref(Company.ContactPhone)">
                    <span class="site-visually-hidden">Anrufen: </span>@Company.ContactPhone
                </a>
            }
        </div>
    </div>
</header>
